        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7f035cd4-6544-5b5a-8603-4dab88bb5a15",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bo Diddley, Ellas McDaniel, Ellas Otha Bates\n- Organizations: The Yardbirds\n- Places: London\n- Roles: singer, guitarist, songwriter, music producer\n- Concepts: R&B, blues, rock and roll, musical influence\n\nFacts:\n- Bo Diddley was born as Ellas Otha Bates on December 30, 1928, and he was also known as Ellas McDaniel.\n- Bo Diddley was an American R&B singer, guitarist, songwriter, and music producer.\n- Bo Diddley played a key role in the transition from the blues to rock and roll.\n- Bo Diddley influenced artists including Elvis Presley, Buddy Holly, the Beatles, the Rolling Stones, the Yardbirds, Eric Clapton, the Who, Jimi Hendrix, George Thorogood, Parliament-Funkadelic, and The Clash.\n- The Yardbirds are an English rock band that was formed in London in 1963.\n- Bo Diddley died on June 2, 2008.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
